# Attributes for the schema and everything rendered from it.
#
# Scoped to `buffers/` and the crate it generates into. Two jobs: keep generated
# and vendored schema code out of the language statistics and collapsed in
# review, and stop git merging a file where a textual merge would be wrong.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Schema languages
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Protocol Buffer is a `data` language in linguist, and data languages are left
# out of the language bar by default. These protos are the API's source of
# truth — the thing most worth seeing in the repository summary — so they are
# opted back in.
*.proto text eol=lf linguist-detectable=true

# The flat renderings. Both are marked generated below, so neither reaches the
# statistics; these lines are about highlighting and line endings.
#
# `.capnp` is left to extension detection, which already resolves it: the
# language's name contains a space and a git attribute value cannot, so writing
# it here would set the language to `Cap'n` and break the thing it was meant to
# fix. `.fbs` is stated because that extension is ambiguous, and an attribute
# naming a language linguist does not know is ignored rather than harmful.
*.capnp text eol=lf
*.fbs   text eol=lf linguist-language=FlatBuffers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated: committed for reproducible builds, not written by hand
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The generated code is committed so `cargo build` needs no protobuf toolchain,
# no capnp and no flatc. That trade only works if review can tell the difference
# between code someone wrote and code a generator emitted — otherwise a
# regenerated tree buries the change that caused it. Marking these collapses
# them in diffs and drops them from the language statistics, which would
# otherwise report far more Rust than anyone has written.
#
# `eol=lf` matters more here than elsewhere: a generator rewrites these files
# wholesale, so a CRLF checkout would show every one as modified the moment
# anybody regenerated on Windows.
#
# Regenerate with `cargo xtask gen-buffers`; CI checks the result matches.
crates/platform/telividb-buffers/src/generated/** text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
crates/platform/telividb-buffers/src/lib.rs       text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
buffers/capnp/**                                  linguist-generated=true
buffers/flatbuffers/**                            linguist-generated=true

# The committed descriptor set, and the copy the renderer reads. Binary, so git
# neither diffs them nor touches their bytes.
crates/platform/telividb-buffers/src/generated/protobuf/descriptor.bin binary
descriptors.binpb                                                      binary

# Protobuf documentation, rendered from the protos by `cargo xtask protodoc`.
buffers/protobuf/**/README.md linguist-generated=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored: other people's schemas, kept for tooling rather than compiled here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copies of the annotation packages, present only so an editor can resolve
# imports. buf resolves them from the registry, so nothing here is compiled —
# see buf.yaml, which excludes the same path.
buffers/protobuf/.deps/** linguist-vendored=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ordinal ledger: never merged textually
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# It records which target slot every field was assigned. A slot is a wire
# format: a consumer compiled against a schema where a field sat at ordinal 5
# reads slot 5 forever. A textual merge would silently pick one branch's
# assignment over the other's, so a conflict here is resolved by regenerating —
# a compatibility decision, not a text edit.
buffers.lock -merge linguist-generated=true
